{
  "id": "Compound::DB01182 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Propafenone is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2d6 through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Propafenone may influence Cyp2d6 via the binding of certain compounds, as indicated by the links to Dolasetron, Etoricoxib, and Rosiglitazone, all of which bind to Cyp2d6. These compounds are themselves downstream effects of Propafenone, which causes changes in physiological parameters such as Monocyte Count Increased, Ketonuria, and Wide Complex Tachycardia. The shared ancestry of Propafenone and these compounds, through the Lowest Common Ancestor (LCA) of Carbonyl Compound, Organonitrogen Compound, and Organic Amino Compound, suggests a broader metabolic or enzymatic context in which Cyp2d6 is involved. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Propafenone may modulate Cyp2d6 activity, though the exact nature of this modulation remains to be fully elucidated.",
